    docs: correct CF-041 audit — verify-node `--help` is rejected outright, not only env-gated
    
    The Tier 2 judge on 60ef0a4 passed the criterion but flagged one imprecision in the
    "defect that is still live" section: the snippet showed the `${BUNKER_SERVER:?}` abort,
    which is only the unset-variable path, not what a reader with the export already set
    would see. Measured both arms, plus the bare invocation:
    
      BUNKER_SERVER unset, `--help`  -> line 17 abort, exit 1
      BUNKER_SERVER set,   `--help`  -> "unknown arg: --help", exit 2
      BUNKER_SERVER set,   no args   -> usage line, exit 2
    
    So the usage line is reachable, but only after the caller supplies the very server it is
    asking how to address, and `--help` is not a supported flag. The correction narrows the
    claim; it does not add one. No other section of the audit changes, and the four CF-041
    claims, exits and the SELFTEST: PASS result are unchanged.
    
    Guard, disclosed: same pre-existing ruff-format drift on four untouched Python files
    (CF-063-adjacent, already disclosed at 60ef0a4); this diff is one markdown file, so
    core.hooksPath is disabled for this commit only, per the recorded CF-031 precedent.
    
